-- title:
--   Lifting a based free algebra with monogenic special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R'$ and $R$ be commutative local rings and let $\pi\colon R'\to R$ be a surjective ring homomorphism. Let $C$ be a commutative $R$-algebra, let $\iota$ be a finite index type, and let $e\colon\iota\to C$ be an $R$-basis of $C$ (so $C$ is free of finite rank over $R$), with a distinguished index $i_0\in\iota$ such that $e_{i_0}=1$. Assume furthermore that $C$ is monogenic modulo the maximal ideal in the following sense: there is $y\in C$ such that for every $z\in C$ there is a polynomial $q\in R[X]$ with $z-q(y)$ lying in $\mathfrak m_R\cdot C$, the submodule generated by products of elements of the maximal ideal of $R$ with elements of $C$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $C'$ in the same universe as $R'$, carrying a commutative ring structure and an $R'$-algebra structure, together with an $R'$-basis $e'\colon\iota\to C'$ indexed by the same set $\iota$, and a ring homomorphism $\sigma\colon C'\to C$, such that $e'_{i_0}=1$, such that $\sigma$ is $\pi$-semilinear on scalars, i.e. $\sigma(\mathrm{algebraMap}_{R'\to C'}(r))=\mathrm{algebraMap}_{R\to C}(\pi(r))$ for all $r\in R'$, and such that $\sigma(e'_i)=e_i$ for every $i\in\iota$.
--
--   This is the lifting step for finite free based algebras along a surjection of local rings: a commutative $R$-algebra that is free with a marked basis and monogenic over the residue data lifts, basis and all, to the ring upstairs, so that the based algebra $(C,e)$ is recovered from $(C',e')$ by applying $\pi$ to the scalars. It is used in the construction of local coboundaries for small extensions in the form [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_local_coboundary_of_smallExtension_of_monogenic_fibre`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_local_coboundary_of_smallExtension_of_monogenic_fibre).
